    {
      "id": "IP23",
      "title": "Retry taxonomy",
      "finding": "Per-file processing retains hard error, soft error and sendBlocked states. A selected network-failure policy permits automatic retries after 1000 and 5000 ms; manual retry clears pending error state. Validation failures and intentional aborts follow separate paths.",
      "classification": "observed_packaged_client_control_flow",
      "conditions": [
        "The retry predicate requires online/not-unloading state, sufficient elapsed attempt time and a classified transport failure.",
        "These delays are not a blanket policy for every upload or every server error."
